+        j*kp+kp-1 >= cached_len (never a radix-shared row), and decode writes at the
+        newest token's row. (At the first-token row a pool straddling a radix-share
+        boundary had its key in the OTHER request's row: scored with a foreign key after
+        the chunk-commit dedup re-point, and rewritten into the tree by a hit ending
+        mid-pool.) Readers: _pool_key_rows (decode scoring, eager +
